# Product copy of Crux's clang-tidy selection. The check list equals Crux's, and a test compares
# the two. Only the header filter differs: it names the directories of a product repository, so
# that headers of Zephyr, Crux and the SDK are not reported. Copy this file to the product root.
#
# clang-tidy needs a compile database. A Zephyr build writes compile_commands.json when
# CMAKE_EXPORT_COMPILE_COMMANDS is on. Crux does not provide one for a product, and nobody has run
# these checks on Zephyr driver sources here, so expect to tune the list for them.
# readability-identifier-naming has no options, so it reports nothing, as in Crux's own file: the
# naming rules of docs/coding-guidelines.md are not enforced by this file.
#
# Keep the C17 enum ABI and explicitly length-checked C library calls; these two
# generic checks flag the language/library form rather than a project defect.
Checks: >-
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.DeprecatedOrUnsafeBufferHandling,
  performance-*,
  -performance-enum-size,
  portability-*,
  readability-identifier-naming
WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*/(app|domain|drivers|include|tests)/.*'
FormatStyle: file
